+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry is the enforcement boundary for the JSON Schema already advertised to AI providers. Invalid model-generated arguments become readable tool results so the model can correct them without terminating the conversation.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- Before invoking an executor, `ToolRegistry.execute` validates required properties, declared types, and enums against the resolved tool definition. A rejection result identifies the property path and failed constraint without including property values in either returned text or logs; valid input, including unlisted properties, reaches the executor unchanged ([validated by: rejects invalid private input before execution and passes valid extra properties through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L23)).
+- A static tool schema is compiled during `register`, so an invalid schema throws an error naming the tool before any conversation begins. Executing an unregistered name remains the separate error `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: rejects a broken schema when registering its named tool and preserves the unknown-tool error](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L65)).
+- A static definition's schema is compiled once and the resulting validation contract is reused across executions ([validated by: keeps using the schema compiled when a static tool was registered](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L86)).
+- A function-valued definition is resolved for each execution and that call is validated against its current schema rather than a schema returned by an earlier resolution ([validated by: validates each function-valued definition against the schema resolved for that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L109)).
+- Schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` to the existing bounded tool loop, allowing the provider to inspect the rejection and issue a corrected call without `processMessage` rejecting ([validated by: returns a rejection to the model so it can correct the call within the tool loop](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L139)).
+
+## Documentation and packaging
+
+The runtime validator is a production dependency. The public README, tool-author guide, repository system specification, changelog, and release migration note describe the validation boundary, unchanged extra properties, retry behavior, and the effect on executors that formerly handled malformed input themselves.
